# resources_gap_placement_delete: A service task with argument buffers takes a placement list (opcode 68). When its lists are first mapped, the task's rebuild reserves objects, walking every entry: a type 7 entry with a nonzero resourceID is reserved only if its record is a sampler (commandType 3), so a depth-stencil record there (commandType 4) and a type 7 entry whose record lies past the task's end reserve nothing. A texture and a buffer with zero entries are made by an exec and write their placement back (a resourceIndex and gpuResourceID, a GPU address: host values). Then deleting either clears its entry: 37 on the texture and 40 (operation 1000) on the buffer each delete the object and clear its placement, which zeroes the entry. An exec makes both again, writing their entries anew. Host-keyed: the written values are the host's.
